        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "\n\nNow let me understand the problem better by looking at how images are currently handled. Based on my analysis:\n\n**Current Issues:**\n1. Each image reference (tag, digest, ID) triggers a separate metadata event\n2. The `Name` field is updated based on simple heuristics but doesn't follow the priority order specified\n3. During initial collection, multiple events can be emitted for the same underlying image\n\n**Required Solution:**\n1. Aggregate all references belonging to the same image (by manifest digest)\n2. Emit only ONE event per unique image after all references are collected\n3. Set the `Name` field with priority: repo digest > repo tag > raw image ID\n4. Update existing image names only when the new name is more readable (no sha256)\n5. Skip images on manifest errors without stopping collection\n6. Respect the `container_image.enabled` config flag\n\nLet me create the implementation:\n\n",
          "time": {
            "start": 1782155256140,
            "end": 1782155256175
          },
          "id": "prt_ef0bb214c001ftppG4uhK8sice",
          "sessionID": "ses_10f4669f8ffee2ZpyjRQgIqSEi",
