          "type": "text",
          "text": "\n\nPerfect! All tests pass. However, I noticed an issue with my implementation - when we have both a repo tag and a repo digest, the `getPreferredName` function should return the repo digest (as per the requirements), but I need to verify the logic is correct. Let me also reconsider the requirement more carefully.\n\nLooking back at the requirements:\n- \"prefer a repository digest if available, otherwise a repository tag, and fall back to the raw image ID only when no other name exists\"\n\nMy current implementation does this correctly. However, I realize there's a subtle issue - when checking if a name is \"more readable\", I should consider that a repo tag (without sha256) is more readable than a repo digest (which contains sha256). Let me refine the logic:\n\n",
