          "text": "\n\nPerfect! Let me create a comprehensive summary of the implementation:\n\n## Summary\n\nI've successfully implemented the image metadata aggregation logic for the containerd runtime collector. Here's what was changed:\n\n### Key Changes\n\n#### 1. **Added `getPreferredName` function** (`image.go:162-181`)\n   - Returns the most user-friendly name for an image based on priority:\n     1. Repository digest (e.g., `gcr.io/datadoghq/agent@sha256:...`)\n     2. Repository tag (e.g., `gcr.io/datadoghq/agent:7`)\n     3. Raw image ID (e.g., `sha256:abc123...`)\n\n#### 2. **Added `isNameMoreReadable` function** (`image.go:183-208`)\n   - Determines if a new name is more readable than an existing one\n   - A name is more readable if:\n     - Old name is a raw image ID and new name is not\n     - Old name is a repo digest and new name is a repo tag\n   - This ensures we only update names when they become more user-friendly\n\n#### 3. **Updated `notifyEventForImage` function** (`image.go:295-368`)\n   - Now aggregates all references (tags and digests) before emitting an event\n   - Adds the current reference to `knownImages`\n   - Retrieves all aggregated repo tags and digests\n   - Selects the preferred name using `getPreferredName`\n   - Checks if the image already exists and only updates the name if the new one is more readable\n   - Emits a single metadata event with all references included\n\n#### 4. **Updated `notifyInitialImageEvents` function** (`containerd.go:278-324`)\n   - Implements a two-pass approach:\n     - **First pass**: Collects all image references and groups them by image ID (manifest digest)\n     - **Second pass**: Emits exactly one event per unique image with all references aggregated\n   - Skips images with manifest errors (logs warning and continues)\n   - Uses a `processedImages` map to ensure each unique image gets only one event\n\n#### 5. **Added imports** (`containerd.go:19-20`)\n   - Added `github.com/containerd/containerd/images` for manifest operations\n   - Added `github.com/containerd/containerd/namespaces` for namespace context\n\n### Tests Added\n\n1. **`TestGetPreferredName`** - Verifies the priority order for selecting image names\n2. **`TestIsNameMoreReadable`** - Tests the readability comparison logic with 8 test cases\n3. **`TestImageAggregation`** - Tests the complete aggregation workflow with multiple references\n\n### Behavior\n\n- **During initial collection**: All image references are collected first, then one event is emitted per unique image with all tags and digests aggregated\n- **During runtime events**: Each event updates the aggregated references and emits a single event\n- **Name selection**: Prefers repo digests > repo tags > raw IDs\n- **Name updates**: Only updates existing image names when the new name is more readable\n- **Error handling**: Manifest errors are logged and the image is skipped, without aborting the entire collection\n- **Feature flag**: Respects the `container_image.enabled` configuration flag\n\nAll existing tests pass, and the new functionality is covered by comprehensive unit tests.",
